A||||4||burdell1||Trunk Release
Z||000000||burdell1||08-11-99||05:51 PM||||I am having a problem with my electronic trunk release. Sometimes it works, but more often than not it doesn't. Where are the wires for it on the rear deck lid. I'm sure they have been cut before and reattached (because I have had some work done to it) but I am not sure where they are.
Z||000001||BOILERMAKER||08-11-99||05:56 PM||||What kind of tranny do you have.  According to the book, the emergency brake has to be pulled in order to complete the circuit and make the trunk release work.  Other than that, there is a relay under the dash.  I can't remember what the colored wires are that go to it, but I had this problem earlier and then I started fiddling with the E-brake and it worked. 
Z||000002||burdell1||08-11-99||06:34 PM||||I've got an '85 GT with automatic transmission.<br>
Z||000003||theogre||08-11-99||07:20 PM||||auto tranny must be in park for the latch to work. If the neutral/start switch is out of whack, it could screw up the latch, but it also tends to screw up starting the car.<p>The relay is under the dash in a clip on the right side of the steering column. swap this relay with the horn relay and see if the latch opens properly. if it does, replace the relay.
Z||000004||burdell1||08-14-99||08:56 AM||||problem solved!! the dip switch for the trunk wasn't being pressed down all the way. I put an little plastic hub on the trunk and presto! works perfect! if anyone has the same problem, try it!<br>
